#
# AMD graphics
#
# Separate from the gpu profile because amdgpu does not work without binary
# firmware, and it does not fall back to an unaccelerated mode the way i915
# does: it refuses to initialise the card if the blobs are absent, and
# nothing then drives the panel but the firmware's framebuffer (simpledrm).
# That framebuffer cannot switch the panel off or bring it back, so without
# amdgpu a sleep leaves the backlight lit and wakes to a blank screen, and an
# APU's graphics are never power managed. The build composes this profile
# always (build.c profiles_always), so every image has amdgpu and the
# firmware for mainstream desktop, laptop, and handheld AMD GPUs and APUs
# (Southern/Sea Islands, Polaris/VI, Vega/Raven/Picasso/Renoir/Cezanne/
# Green Sardine, Van Gogh, and RDNA 1/2/3/3.5/4), excluding Instinct server
# accelerators and ISP camera blobs (~29.7 MiB zstd compressed across 645 files).
#
# No blob is in git. The lines below name each file with its SHA-256 at the
# linux-firmware commit kernel/firmware/apply pins, and the build fetches
# them (see the wifi profile for how they reach the initramfs).
#
#> firmware amdgpu/banks_k_2_smc.bin bcdaef2cbec1b21d8d83d6e03d245ccee7fd3052b4a0ab88601b4dad392991dd
#> firmware amdgpu/beige_goby_ce.bin 13aecf0a22dbc3071ade01355b27a4f90a0f46fc699064ab63e08392e65bbeab
